From f110b25e75ec42071a73f6238efafbc8f7be5f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:20:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 108/115] ASoC: wcd934x: parse the mic bias voltages from the
 devicetree

Converting the driver to the shared wcd helper moved the mic bias
voltages into struct wcd_common and deleted wcd934x_get_micbias_val(),
which used to read them out of the devicetree. The same change added the
wcd_dt_parse_micbias_info() call to wcd937x, wcd938x and wcd939x, but
not to wcd934x -- so common.micb_vout[] and common.micb_mv[] are never
populated and keep the zeroes they were allocated with.

wcd934x_init_dmic() then programs ANA_MICB1..4 with a vout_ctl of 0,
which is 1000 mV rather than the 1800 mV every board asks for, and the
MBHC configuration gets a micbias of 0 mV.

On boards whose digital microphones take their supply from the codec's
mic bias outputs this is the difference between a working microphone and
silence: at 1000 mV the DMIC does not run, its data line never toggles,
and the decimator sees a constant that the TX high-pass filter removes,
so capture returns a brief settling transient followed by samples that
are exactly zero. Measured on a Google Pixel 2 XL: ANA_MICB1..4 all read
0x00 where the pre-conversion driver left them at 0x10.

Parse the values in probe, as the other three codecs do.

Fixes: 4f16b6351bbf ("ASoC: codecs: wcd: add common helper for wcd codecs")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index bcd249024e43..864812be80f6 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -6057,6 +6057,10 @@ static int wcd934x_codec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	wcd->common.dev = dev->parent;
 	wcd->common.max_bias = 4;
 
+	ret = wcd_dt_parse_micbias_info(&wcd->common);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = wcd934x_codec_parse_data(wcd);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
